  "explanation": {
    "short": "A dot under a letter slightly changes its sound. ज़ is the \"z\" of बाज़ार, फ़ is the \"f\" of फ़ोन, and ड़ is a quick flap of the tongue, a little like a fast \"r\": बड़ा, लड़का.",
    "more": "ज़ and फ़ are found in words that came from Persian, Arabic and English; some speakers say ज and फ instead, and everyone understands. ड़ is never at the start of a word. In लड़का the middle \"a\" is not said: laṛ-kā."
  },
